<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Ninian &amp; Lester yr eps, div knocked.</title>
<headline>Ninian &amp; Lester yr eps, div knocked.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996. (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     258	   vs 303</p>
<p>    Final div (cts)	  75	   vs  87</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   9.63	  vs 10.73</p>
<p>    Income after tax	10.75	 vs 11.92</p>
<p>    Income before tax     15.88	 vs 17.87</p>
<p>    Tax			 5.13	  vs 5.95</p>
<p>    Interest		  4.34	  vs 6.43</p>
<p>    Turnover		  328.64	vs 324.06</p>
<p>Div payable April 23.</p>
<p>On register March 20 for div.</p>
<p>Full name: Ninian &amp; Lester Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said they would award capitalisation shares. They said, however, instead of capitalisation award sharholders may in respect of all or part of their shareholdings elect to receive a final cash dividend of 75 cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
